-- title:
--   Switcheroo Second Aggregate Term Close
-- statement:
--   **The second positive switcheroo term is within twice the self-consistency square root of its common center.**
--
--   Let `psi_bi` be normalized and assume complete G self consistency at level `zeta`. Denote the second aggregate term by $T_2$, and denote by $C$ the average middle-sandwich expectation built from the complete-part projection family and the total of the `M` submeasurement. Then
--
--   $$
--   \left|T_2-C\right|\le2\sqrt{\zeta}.
--   $$
--
--   The generic complete-part self-consistency lemma supplies the switcheroo relation used here. This bound closes the second positive term against the common center that is later rewritten as an operator-tensor average.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.switcheroo_second_aggregate_term_close`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
